3. Data and assets
------------------

Test art
  benchmark/cases.mjs and scripts/test-targets.mjs draw all test art
  from shapes, with a fixed seed. No third-party images. Covered by the
  MIT License.

src/assets/brand/
  The tool marks shared with the Separation Table, made by ADN. The
  PNGs and favicon.ico are rendered from the SVGs. The ADN name and
  logo are trademarks of American Dream Network and are not covered by
  the MIT License grant.

Printer and RIP product names (CADlink, AcroRIP, Maintop, Epson
Garment Creator) are named only to say which software loads the
files. No vendor files, profiles or documentation are copied in.
Product names are trademarks of their owners.

Fonts: none bundled.


4. Published methods implemented here or in the engine
------------------------------------------------------

  CIEDE2000 colour difference: Sharma, Wu and Dalal, "The CIEDE2000
    color-difference formula", Color Research and Application, 2005
    (Separation Table engine)
  Area-exact halftone dots and ordered 8x8 Bayer thresholds
    (Separation Table engine)
  MaxRects rectangle packing with the bottom-left and other placement
    rules: Jukka Jylanki, "A Thousand Ways to Pack the Bin", 2010
    (src/nest.js). Implemented from the paper; no third-party code is
    ported. rectpack, which the benchmark runs, is not used by the tool.
